{
  "_readme": [
    "Hardcore Region Difficulty - quality definitions. Edit, delete or add entries; then run /hrd quality reload (or just save: the server reloads it automatically).",
    "Each category (weapon, tool, armor, ranged, shield) has its own list. Delete an entry to remove that quality. An empty list [] disables qualities for that category. A missing category uses the built-in defaults.",
    "id: unique per category, A-Z 0-9 _ only (stored on items). name: optional display name (plain text or a lang key); without it the lang file / the id is used.",
    "color: a vanilla color name (gold, dark_purple, aqua, ...) or a hex code like #FF8800.",
    "tier: whole number from tier_min to tier_max (default -5..5, change both below). Used for sorting and for the default weight_group (negative < 0, neutral = 0, positive = 1, high >= 2). Optional. A tier outside the limits is clamped. The quality with tier 0 is the 'standard' one (villagers at a low level sell it).",
    "weight: relative roll chance (only the ratio inside a category matters; the in-game editor shows it as a % and saves % x 100, e.g. 12.5% = 1250). weight_group: negative (less likely in dangerous regions), neutral (unchanged), positive (more likely), high (more likely, uses high_tier_bonus_multiplier).",
    "Weights are only used by loot / mob drops / villagers / inventory (scaled by the region or villager level). The Quality Forge and crafted / inventory items ignore weights and levels: the chance depends only on the tier (your own qualities are balanced automatically: the share of a tier is split equally between all qualities of that tier; standard is the likeliest, bad qualities are likelier than good ones, higher tier = rarer; Mythic, Divine, Flawless included), and Luck (Potion of Luck, luck_quality_bonus in the config) tilts it toward the good ones. An old forge_weight is ignored.",
    "unlock_level: for weight 0 entries in group high: appears from that difficulty level if 'unlock_high_qualities' is on. 0 = never.",
    "effects: percents are fractions (0.10 = +10%); armor_bonus / reach are flat. Only the keys listed for the category are used (weapon: damage, attack_speed, durability, reach | tool: damage, attack_speed, durability, mining_speed, reach | armor: armor, durability, armor_bonus | ranged: arrow_damage, draw_speed, durability | shield: durability, armor_bonus, move_speed, hold_mining). Other keys are ignored.",
    "strict_limits: true = clamp percents to -0.20..+0.20, reach to -0.5..+0.5 and armor_bonus to -0.5..+1.5 (the original balance limits)."
  ],
  "strict_limits": false,
  "tier_min": -5,
  "tier_max": 5,
